{
  "manifest_version": "1",
  "ys_version": "0.2.8",
  "comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the probe suite. Adding a probe is a data edit",
    "here plus a corpus and an expected file - never a new script.",
    "Paths are repo-relative.",
    "",
    "invoke: 'run'   -> ys FILE       (programs that print via say:)",
    "invoke: 'print' -> ys -p FILE    (programs that evaluate to a value)",
    "Getting this wrong does not error, it compares the wrong output.",
    "",
    "match comes from the expected file: an 'expected_output' key compares",
    "exactly, an 'expected_output_contains' key requires every listed substring.",
    "",
    "status: 'xfail' marks a probe that is expected to FAIL - a known, open",
    "defect kept under observation rather than an accepted ERROR. It reports",
    "XFAIL while it fails and XPASS once it passes, and XPASS fails the run, so",
    "fixing a defect forces the entry to be retired rather than left to rot.",
    "No entry carries it at the moment: the two that did (the `let` binding",
    "form and map-literal keys) were fixed and retired on 2026-10-17, which is",
    "what XPASS is for. Probes that fail now fail loudly.",
    "",
    "v1.1.0's corpus lives under probes_v1_1/ rather than probes/ so those",
    "frozen files stay byte-identical and in place; the manifest references",
    "them explicitly. Fold them in under a new suite version when convenient.",
    "v1.2.0 follows the same convention under probes_v1_2/, and v1.3.0 under",
    "probes_v1_3/."
  ],
